      "package": "rsa",
      "version": "0.9.10",
      "id": "RUSTSEC-2023-0071",
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "The selected Windows graph reaches rsa only through librespot-core. Its sole production use imports RsaPublicKey, BigUint and Pkcs1v15Sign, then verifies the server handshake signature with a public modulus/exponent. Lime does not create an RSA private key or call RSA private-key decryption/signing. The Marvin private-key timing leak therefore has no secret private key or vulnerable private operation in this application path. This assessment is limited to the pinned feature graph and reviewed source hashes; it is not an upstream patch.",
      "references": [
        "https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2023-0071.html"
      ]
    }
  ],
